                s("Conflict Resolution Order (PMI Preference)", "• Collaborate / Problem Solve ✅ — ALWAYS try first; win-win; addresses root cause\n• Compromise / Reconcile — each party gives something; good when full collaboration not possible\n• Smooth / Accommodate — downplay differences; emphasise agreement; temporary only\n• Force / Direct — one party wins; only in genuine emergencies\n• Withdraw / Avoid ❌ — almost always wrong; never a long-term solution"),
                s("Power Types (PMI Preference Order)", "• Expert Power ✅ — most sustainable; does not depend on title\n• Referent Power ✅ — built through trust and relationships over time\n• Reward Power — effective but use carefully; avoid creating dependency\n• Legitimate / Formal Power — authority without influence is limited\n• Penalty / Coercive Power ❌ — damages trust and psychological safety; avoid"),
                s("Contract Types — Risk Summary", tableHeaders = listOf("Contract Type", "Risk: Buyer", "Risk: Seller", "Best Scope Scenario"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("FFP (Firm Fixed Price)", "Low", "High", "Well-defined, stable requirements"), listOf("FPIF", "Low-Medium", "Medium", "Defined scope; want to incentivise"), listOf("FPEPA", "Low-Medium", "Medium", "Long-term; price fluctuations expected"), listOf("CPFF", "High", "Low", "Uncertain scope; R&D"), listOf("CPIF", "High", "Low-Medium", "Long projects; incentivise efficiency"), listOf("T&M", "Medium", "Medium", "Unclear scope; short-term; staff aug."))),
                s("Key Document Guide", tableHeaders = listOf("Document", "When to Use It", "First Action When Needed"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Project Charter", "High-level guidance needed; authorise project", "Created by Sponsor in Initiating"), listOf("Project Management Plan", "Detailed guidance on any management topic", "Reference before any significant decision"), listOf("Issue Log", "Problem has ALREADY occurred", "Update Issue Log FIRST, then take action"), listOf("Risk Register", "Uncertain event MIGHT happen in future", "Document risk → Analyze → Plan response"), listOf("Lessons Learned Register", "Capture knowledge throughout project", "Update when issues resolved AND at closure"), listOf("Change Log", "Track all change requests", "Create change request → submit to CCB"), listOf("Assumption Log", "Track assumptions and constraints", "Update throughout planning and execution"), listOf("Stakeholder Register", "Manage stakeholder information and strategy", "Created in Initiating; updated throughout"))),
                s("Motivation Theory Quick Reference", tableHeaders = listOf("Theory", "Key Insight", "Hygiene vs. Motivator"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Maslow", "5 levels: Physio → Safety → Social → Esteem → Self-Actualisation. Lower needs first.", "N/A — hierarchical needs"), listOf("Herzberg", "Hygiene factors prevent dissatisfaction; Motivators create satisfaction. TWO DIFFERENT SCALES.", "Hygiene: salary, conditions, security. Motivators: achievement, recognition, growth."), listOf("McGregor", "X: people dislike work (directive). Y: people are self-motivated (empowering). PMI prefers Y.", "N/A — leadership style theory"), listOf("McClelland", "Three needs: Achievement, Affiliation, Power. Match role to dominant need.", "N/A — needs-based theory"), listOf("Vroom Expectancy", "Motivation = Expectancy × Instrumentality × Valence. All three must be present.", "N/A — process theory"))),
                s("Organisational Structure — PM Authority", tableHeaders = listOf("Structure", "PM Authority", "Resource Control"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Organic / Functional / Multi-divisional", "Little or none", "Functional Manager"), listOf("Matrix — Weak", "Low", "Functional Manager dominant"), listOf("Matrix — Balanced", "Moderate", "Shared"), listOf("Matrix — Strong / Project-oriented", "High to almost total", "Project Manager"), listOf("PMO", "High to almost total", "PMO / Project Manager"))),
                s("The Golden Rules for Exam Day", "• 🔑 A.R.T.: Assess → Review → Take Action. Never jump to action first.\n• 🔑 ALL changes = ICC. No exceptions, no matter who asks.\n• 🔑 Safety first. Stop all work. Always.\n• 🔑 Risk = register. Issue = issue log. Know the difference.\n• 🔑 Collaborate before escalating. Escalate only when beyond your authority.\n• 🔑 Team estimates. PM does not estimate for the team.\n• 🔑 Acceptance before transition. Get formal sign-off before operations.\n• 🔑 Closure sequence: Accept → Lessons Learned → Transition → Disband.\n• 🔑 Face-to-face for conflict. Always the preferred communication method.\n• 🔑 Sprint changes go to backlog. Protect the Sprint Goal always.\n• 🔑 Servant leadership. PM serves the team — team does not serve the PM.\n• 🔑 Absolute terms trap. \"Always/never/only/all\" in an option = usually wrong."),
                s("Worked example — 📖 Quick Scenario → Answer Reference", "PEOPLE DOMAIN SCENARIOS:\n\nTeam member upset / struggling → Private 1:1 conversation first. Understand root cause. Servant leadership.\n\nTeam in conflict → Meet individually → Bring together → Collaborate. Escalate only if authority issue.\n\nNew team member joins → Team may regress to Forming/Storming. Update team charter. Facilitate integration.\n\nRetrospective is silent → Low psychological safety. Use anonymous input. Model vulnerability.\n\nTeam always says \"yes\" in standups, then misses goals → Safety issue. People hiding bad news.\n\nSenior team member dismisses juniors → Address privately. PMI Code — Respect mandatory standard.\n\nPM needs to influence without authority → Expert power + reciprocity + framing in their interest.\n\nTeam member unmotivated despite good salary → Herzberg: hygiene factor met. Add motivators (recognition, growth, meaningful work).\n\nPROCESS DOMAIN SCENARIOS:\n\nProject behind schedule → Assess critical path → Fast track first (free) → Crash if needed (costs more).\n\nSponsor wants to bypass change control → Still submit formal change request. No exceptions.\n\nRisk occurs with no contingency plan → Implement workaround (unplanned response). Update lessons learned.\n\nDefect found after customer accepted → Defect repair change request → Fix → Regression test → Re-validate.\n\nRequirements disputed at acceptance → Check the Scope Baseline and RTM. Was the requirement baselined and traced?\n\nCPI Identify which formula: typical (BAC/CPI), atypical (AC + BAC−EV), or flawed (AC + bottom-up).\n\nSprint velocity dropping → Check for impediments, context switching, team changes. Scrum Master removes blockers.\n\nBUSINESS ENVIRONMENT SCENARIOS:\n\nNew regulation impacts project → It's a certainty (not just risk). Assess → Change request → Comply. No exemptions.\n\nBusiness case becomes invalid mid-project → Reassess → Present to sponsor → Sponsor decides continue/modify/terminate.\n\nBenefits not realised post-project → Benefits Owner drives realisation. PM's job is transitioning with tracking in place.\n\nAI tool gives wrong recommendation → PM validates. PM is accountable. AI augments — never decides.\n\nStakeholder resistant to change → ADKAR: identify barrier (usually Desire). Address root cause, not symptom.\n\nProject delivers outputs but no value → PMBOK 8: project failed. Outputs ≠ outcomes. Adoption + impact = success.", SectionKind.TIP),
                s("All Formulas — Complete Reference Card", tableHeaders = listOf("Formula", "Expression", "Key Variables", "Interpretation"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("EV", "% Complete × BAC", "BAC=Budget at Completion", "Dollar value of work actually done"), listOf("SV", "EV − PV", "PV=Planned Value", "Negative=behind schedule. Positive=ahead."), listOf("CV", "EV − AC", "AC=Actual Cost", "Negative=over budget. Positive=under budget."), listOf("SPI", "EV ÷ PV", "—", "1=ahead, =1=on track"), listOf("CPI", "EV ÷ AC", "—", "1=under budget, =1=on budget"), listOf("EAC (typical)", "BAC ÷ CPI", "—", "Variances will continue at current rate"), listOf("EAC (atypical)", "AC + (BAC − EV)", "—", "One-time variance; rest at planned rate"), listOf("EAC (flawed)", "AC + Bottom-up ETC", "ETC=Estimate to Complete", "Replan from scratch"), listOf("EAC (combined)", "AC + (BAC−EV)÷(CPI×SPI)", "—", "Both cost and schedule affect remaining work"), listOf("ETC", "EAC − AC", "—", "Remaining cost to complete"), listOf("VAC", "BAC − EAC", "—", "Negative=will be over budget at completion"), listOf("TCPI (to BAC)", "(BAC−EV)÷(BAC−AC)", "—", ">1=must work more efficiently than now"), listOf("TCPI (to EAC)", "(BAC−EV)÷(EAC−AC)", "—", "Efficiency needed to meet revised estimate"), listOf("PERT Expected", "(O+4M+P)÷6", "O=Optimistic M=MostLikely P=Pessimistic", "Weighted average with most-likely at 4×"), listOf("PERT Std Dev", "(P−O)÷6", "—", "Spread of estimates"), listOf("PERT Variance", "((P−O)÷6)²", "—", "Square of std deviation"), listOf("Communication Channels", "n×(n−1)÷2", "n=number of stakeholders", "Non-linear growth — 10 people=45; 20=190; 50=1225"), listOf("EMV", "Probability × Impact", "—", "Expected Monetary Value; negative for threats"), listOf("PTA", "((Ceiling−Target Price)÷Buyer Share)+Target Cost", "FPIF contracts only", "Actual cost above which seller absorbs all overruns"), listOf("PCE", "VA Time÷Lead Time×100%", "VA=Value Added", "Percentage of total time that adds customer value"), listOf("WSJF", "Cost of Delay÷Job Size", "—", "Weighted Shortest Job First; higher=do first"), listOf("BCR", "PV of Benefits÷PV of Costs", "—", ">1=viable; higher=more attractive"), listOf("ROI", "(Net Benefit−Cost)÷Cost×100%", "—", "Return as % of investment"), listOf("Payback Period", "Investment÷Annual Benefit", "—", "Years to recover investment"))),
                s("Process Sequence — 15 Critical Sequences to Memorise", tableHeaders = listOf("Sequence", "Correct Order", "Common Confusion"), tableRows = listOf(listOf("Scope Baseline Creation", "Scope Statement → WBS → WBS Dictionary", "Cannot build WBS without scope statement; cannot write dictionary without WBS"), listOf("Quality → Acceptance", "Control Quality (team verifies) → Verified Deliverables → Validate Scope (customer accepts) → Accepted Deliverables", "Students confuse Control Quality with Validate Scope — CQ is internal, VS is external (customer)"), listOf("Project Closure", "Formal Acceptance → Lessons Learned → Release Team → Archive Documents → Close Contracts", "Never release team before formal acceptance; never archive before lessons learned"), listOf("Change Control", "Identify need → Submit CR → Impact Analysis → CCB Review → Decision → Update Plan → Communicate → Implement → Monitor", "No shortcuts — all steps required even under time pressure"), listOf("Risk Process", "Identify → Qualitative Analysis → Quantitative Analysis (if needed) → Plan Responses → Implement → Monitor", "Qualitative always happens; Quantitative only for high-priority risks on significant projects"), listOf("WPD→WPI→WPR", "Work Performance DATA (raw, executing) → Work Performance INFO (analyzed, M&C) → Work Performance REPORT (formatted for stakeholders)", "DATA is raw; INFO is analyzed; REPORT is packaged for communication"), listOf("Procurement Flow", "Plan → Conduct (issue RFP, evaluate, award) → Control (manage performance) → Close", "Bidder conference happens in CONDUCT, not Plan"), listOf("Stakeholder Engagement", "Identify → Plan → Engage → Monitor", "Continuous — revisit identification whenever project context changes significantly"), listOf("Team Development", "Form Team → Define Charter → Storming through Performing → Adjourn", "Skip forming stage activities = team stuck in storming"), listOf("Benefits Realisation", "Project Outputs → Business Outcomes → Benefits → Value", "Project team owns Outputs; Benefits Owner owns Outcomes through Value"), listOf("Conflict Resolution", "Meet individually → Bring together → Facilitate collaborative resolution → Escalate if authority issue", "Meeting individually first is almost always the first step"), listOf("Issue vs Risk", "Risk = future uncertainty → Risk Register. Issue = current reality → Issue Log", "Exam tests this distinction constantly: \"may happen\" vs \"has happened\""), listOf("Corrective vs Preventive", "Corrective = fix current deviation from plan. Preventive = prevent future negative event.", "Both require change requests if they affect baselines"), listOf("Primary vs Secondary Risk", "Primary = identified risk. Secondary = new risk created by implementing the response.", "Secondary risks must be added to the risk register and managed"), listOf("EAC Formula Selection", "Read the clue: \"typical/continues\" → BAC/CPI. \"One-time/atypical\" → AC+(BAC-EV). \"Flawed estimate\" → AC+ETC. \"Both indices\" → AC+(BAC-EV)/(CPI×SPI)", "Most common exam mistake: always using BAC/CPI regardless of the scenario"))),
                s("Exam Day — Final Checklist and Mind Tricks", "• First 5 minutes: Write all formulas on scratch paper BEFORE reading Q1. EVM suite, PERT, Channels, PTA, PCE, WSJF.\n• Read questions: Last sentence FIRST — that is what is actually being asked. Then read the full scenario.\n• Eliminate: Remove options that are reactive (not proactive), that escalate prematurely, that bypass process, or that blame team members.\n• Two options remaining: Ask — which is more PROACTIVE? More COLLABORATIVE? More PROCESS-following? More ETHICAL? That one is likely correct.\n• Pacing: 240 min ÷ 180 questions = 1 min 20 sec each. At 1 min 25 sec you would need 255 min — 15 min more than you have. Flag hard questions and return — do not get stuck.\n• \"FIRST\" questions: Always ASSESS before acting. Answer = assess/review/communicate.\n• \"BEST\" questions: Only one option is PMI-aligned. Look for the systematic, process-following, stakeholder-inclusive answer.\n• Change requests: If anything changes the scope/schedule/cost/quality baseline → change request required, no exceptions.\n• Business Environment: Regulatory change = mandatory compliance change request. No debate about whether to comply.\n• Safety: STOP all work immediately if safety is at risk. Nothing — not the schedule, not the sponsor, not the contract — overrides safety."),
